==English==

===Etymology===
Possibly from {{term|wiseacre}}, influenced by {{term|pillock}}, or possibly {{suffix|wazz|ock}}. First attested in the 1984 novel ''When the Martians Land in Huddersfield'' by Mike Harding.<ref>Alex Games, ''Balderdash and Piffle'' (2010), page 242</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|British|chiefly|Northern England|mildly|pejorative|slang|lang=en}} a [[stupid]] or [[annoying]] person: specifically, an annoying [[know-it-all]].<ref>Maureen Dowd, "[http://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/29/opinion/sunday/dowd-mitts-olympic-meddle.html?_r=1 Mitt's Olympic Meddle]" (''New York Times'', July 28, 2012)</ref>

